    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's not just about the technical stuff though, it's the betrayal. they knew i was the one who actually understood the frequency modulation and the nostalgic textures that everyone is copying now. they saw i had the vision and decided it was easier to bury me than to pay me. i want the manifesto to make people realize that everything they love about the genre right now is a hollowed out version of what i created. how do i frame this so it doesn't just sound like i'm complaining, but like i'm the rightful owner of the culture they're all consuming?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
